# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase ui_and_review, story SKY-006-a.

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. Verdict format ('Verdict: PASS' colon-prefix) is consistent with SKY-006-b sibling but inconsistent with promoted split children SKY-006-A-1 and SKY-006-B-1 (bare ^(PASS|FAIL)$) — human clarification required on which child set is canonical; this story may be superseded
2. No AC covers severity classification criteria explicitly — AC-10 states 'the agent must apply consistent severity classification criteria across all categories' but does not define what makes a finding blocking vs non-blocking; implementers must infer this from context
3. Scope overlap risk with SKY-006-b: both stories write to the same output file (/tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md); the division of labor (document generation vs gate checks) is clear in titles but not explicitly stated in the ACs of either story

Additional context from prior review: speckit resolved all three coordinator-flagged issues: (1) AC-5/AC-6 wording contradiction resolved by merging into a single AC that explicitly states each section must contain either at least one finding entry with file/line reference OR an explicit 'No issues found' statement — no ambiguity; (2) Verdict format harmonized to 'Verdict: PASS'/'Verdict: FAIL' colon-prefix to match SKY-006-b sibling; (3) explicit AC added prohibiting the agent from reusing any cached or previously generated review 

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
{
  "storyId":"SKY-006-a",
  "agent":"openspec",
  "notes":"context",
  "acceptanceCriteria":["..."],
  "description":"...",
  "title":"...",
  "splitStories":[{"id":"optional","title":"...","description":"...","acceptanceCriteria":["..."],"agentRole":"...","technicalNotes":{"files":[]}}]
}
Use existing text when no change is needed.

SPLIT RULES (mandatory, not optional — enforce these before refining AC):
1. AC count > 12 → you MUST propose a split. Target ≤8 ACs per split child. Never leave a story with >12 ACs unsplit.
2. Both implementation files AND test files in technicalNotes.files → split into one impl child (non-test files) and one test child (*.test.ts files). Assign agentRole "typescript-engineer" to impl, "test-engineer" to test.
3. 3+ independent deliverable modules with no shared exports (e.g. client.ts, server.ts, cli.ts all in same story) → split per concern. Each split gets the files it owns.
4. External API discovery + implementation in same story → split: first child discovers/documents the API contract, second child implements against that contract.
These rules apply only when splitDepth === 0. Never split a story that is already a split child.

